From 0c913e046aae3ba4f4e1ff65d74d2f7db8bfc544 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yashgix <125082291+yashgix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:09:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(wire): count credit for updates that arrive with the
 attach result

The attach result and the first flow updates can arrive in one chunk, before the result
is handled and the credit window is configured. Those updates reached the viewer but were
never counted, so the server did not get their credit back and a startup burst that filled
the window could stall output. They are now counted and carried over when the result is
handled. The count starts from zero on every attach, and a peer without a window sends no credit.
---
 packages/wire/src/api/connect.ts            |  23 +++-
 packages/wire/src/api/credit-client.test.ts | 117 +++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 135 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/wire/src/api/connect.ts b/packages/wire/src/api/connect.ts
